<http://data.silknow.org/object/ad0d1f89-11b3-3952-90ed-32ee591a8cb6>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Man’s circular cloak of brown ribbed worsted, lined with brown worsted twill, with a 5½-inch (14 cm) cape [flat collar].  The cape, front edges, and lower edges of the centre back seam are embroidered with partially and fully wrapped silver and silver gilt filé and purl, couched in a pattern of large scrolling stems and abstract flowers and leaves.  The neck is bound with ⅞-inch (2.1 cm) wide woven lace [braid] of brown silk and silver filé, with a frog and tassel on the right side and a loop on the left for fastening."@en , "Man's cloak, 1660-79, British; Brown worsted, embroidered with silver and silver-gilt thread"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/399b340f-a29a-3672-835f-7129528d3e49> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/de9cda61-6dc0-3206-b01d-c34c7ecc6edf> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Man’s circular cloak of brown ribbed worsted, lined with brown worsted twill, with a 5½-inch (14 cm) cape [flat collar].  The cape, front edges, and lower edges of the centre back seam are embroidered with partially and fully wrapped silver and silver gilt filé and purl, couched in a pattern of large scrolling stems and abstract flowers and leaves.  The neck is bound with ⅞-inch (2.1 cm) wide woven lace [braid] of brown silk and silver filé, with a frog and tassel on the right side and a loop on the left for fastening."@en , "Man's cloak, 1660-79, British; Brown worsted, embroidered with silver and silver-gilt thread"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/ad0d1f89-11b3-3952-90ed-32ee591a8cb6/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.62-1978" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O13922> .

